## 6. CUTLASS/CuTe vs portable PTX

| Component | Mostly | Notes |
|-----------|--------|-------|
| **`mask.h`, `block.h`** | Portable logic | CuTe tensor layouts; `cutlass::FastDivmod`; `__shfl_sync`, `__viaddmin_s32` |
| **`softmax.h`** | **Portable** | `exp2f`, `__logf`, warp reductions; CuTe tensor views only |
| **`apply_softcap`** | Portable | `cutlass::fast_tanh` (can swap for `tanhf`) |
| **`paged_kv.h`** | **Mostly portable** | `SM80_CP_ASYNC_CACHEGLOBAL_ZFILL` (= `cp.async.cg.shared.global`), `__shfl_sync`, int64 pointer math |
| **`mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp`** | **CUTLASS-heavy** | CuTe TMA descriptors, `cute::GMMA` WGMMA, `cutlass::pipeline`, mbarriers, warp-group sync |
| **`flash_fwd_kernel_sm90.h`** | Orchestration | Warp-specialized producer/consumer; named barriers |
| **`flash_fwd_launch_template.h`** | CUTLASS | `cutlass::kernel_launch`, arch tags |

**Practical port boundary:** You can reimplement `mask.h`, `block.h`, `softmax.h`, `apply_softcap`, and **`PagedKVManager` gather** with raw cp.async + shfl. The **mainloop** (TMA Q/K/V pipelining, WGMMA QK/PV, warp-group overlap, shared-memory layouts) is the CUTLASS rewrite surface per FA3.md.

---

## Quick reference: config → kernel variant

| Config | Key flags | hdim128 decode tiles | KV load |
|--------|-----------|----------------------|---------|
| Gemma2: softcap + SWA + s_aux | `Is_local`, `Has_softcap`, `ptr_S_aux` | N/A (use hdim256: 128×64) | Dense TMA |
| Paged KV page=32 | `PagedKVNonTMA=true` | kBlockM=64 or 128, **kBlockN=128** | cp.async gather |
| Causal decode q=1 | Often `is_causal=false` after special case (`flash_api.cpp:842-846`) | kBlockN=128 if paged+hdim128 | — |

**Pipeline order (all variants):** QK → softcap → mask → online softmax → PV → finalize(_aux) → LSE/O.

